{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1191905-mapuche-pantheon","id":1191905,"title":"Mapuche Pantheon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-05T06:11:41-08:00","id":1191905,"title":"Mapuche Pantheon","content":"The Ngen, the Mapuche deities, are easily among the pantheons I find most confusing. The reason for this is strange; I've seen figures, such as Pillan, listed as singular deities in some sources and categories of deities in others. I'm not sure what to make of this pantheon, and I haven't found any sources online that describe them comprehensively, which is a shame because I really want to use them. Patagonia is essentially barren of pantheons I've found researchable besides the Ngen, and South America as a whole only seems to have the Inca and Guarani available as major pantheons, and maybe the Tupari and Muisca in terms of minor ones, plus a few oddball figures like Ai Apaeac and Sinaa. So I was wondering if anyone on here knew this pantheon well and could give me the rundown of them or at least point me in the right direction for information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T14:18:46-08:00","id":1192058,"title":"","content":"I'd be very interested in the Mapuche and their gods, but I haven't had the time to research them properly yet. Maybe the explanations here might help you get started? <a href=\"https://books.google.de/books?id=i7knIrkToqAC&amp;lpg=PA50&amp;ots=hPDspF3LHF&amp;dq=mapuche%20pantheon&amp;hl=de&amp;pg=PA49#v=onepage&amp;q&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">https://books.google.de/books?id=i7k...page&amp;q&amp;f=false</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T14:52:03-08:00","id":1192069,"title":"","content":"If you speak Spanish, there are a lot of articles on the internet, though. A scholar called Mar\u00eda Ester Grebe seems to have expanded on the above account, and there are a lot of her articles floating around online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:04:05-08:00","id":1192385,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Sacerdos. That book looks like a good place to start. Unfortunately, I can't read Spanish.<br /> <br /> Hmm. It looks like most aspects of nature are ruled over by husband/wife pairs rather than singular deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}